From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:56:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sessions): a delete moves the chat to a trash for 7 days

With sessions.trash_days above 0 (default 7; 0 = delete at once, upstream's behavior), every delete path hides the chat instead of removing it: `hermes sessions delete`, the gateway/hub delete (session.mutate delete), bulk delete, `sessions prune`, `sessions clean` and the housekeeping prune. A trashed session and its delegate or compression children keep every row (messages, FTS entries, usage, system prompts, pin); a marker in state_meta hides them from session lists, counts, search, id and title resolves, peer recovery, boot restore and the live list, and fences new admissions. `hermes sessions trash` lists them (id, title, deleted, messages, purge time); `hermes sessions restore <id>` brings one back with its children and pin. A purge hard-deletes after trash_days, on the next delete or housekeeping pass; `hermes sessions delete --purge <id>` deletes one at once. Plugins and memory providers (on_session_delete) hear about a chat only when it is purged. Bulk deletes print how many went to the trash and how to restore.
